# Table Columns Pattern

For simple tables where `row.original` is the full entity (current DataTable), accessor columns are fine:

```typescript
import type { ColumnDef } from "@tanstack/react-table";
import type { Users } from "@/lib/common/ds/types/admin/Users";

export function getColumns(handlers: {
  onEdit: (user: Users) => void;
}): ColumnDef<Users>[] {
  return [
    { accessorKey: "name", header: "Name" },
    { accessorKey: "email", header: "Email" },
    {
      id: "actions",
      cell: ({ row }) => (
        <ActionsCell user={row.original} onEdit={handlers.onEdit} />
      ),
    },
  ];
}
```

## When using store-reactive cells

If a cell must re-render when a single field changes without remounting the row, prefer `useRowValue`:

```typescript
import { useRowValue } from "@/lib/common/store";
import type { Store } from "@/lib/common/store";

function NameCell({ store, rowId }: { store: Store<Users>; rowId: string }) {
  const name = useRowValue(store, rowId, "name");
  return <span>{name ?? "—"}</span>;
}
```

## Dates

Format date-only values with UTC or local-parse helpers — see `date-handling.mdc`. Avoid `new Date('YYYY-MM-DD').toLocaleDateString()` without timezone care.
